# Demo-only overrides for the Spark compose stack (deploy/spark/docker-compose.yml). No secrets here.
# The production default is WARROOM_DEMO_CONTROLS=0: /api/sim/* (scenario, speed, step, the demo key row and the
# trigger menu) is refused on a real line. For a stage demo or deploy/spark/smoke_access.sh, layer this file
# over the box's .env (the later --env-file wins):
#   cd /opt/warroom/current/deploy/spark
#   docker compose --env-file .env --env-file ../spark-demo/compose-demo.env up -d app
# or for one start:  WARROOM_DEMO_CONTROLS=1 docker compose up -d app
# Back to production: plain `docker compose up -d app` (or systemctl restart warroom-stack).
# run_warroom_spark.sh (the venv run on :8090) does not use compose; it reads ~/.westie/warroom.env instead.
WARROOM_DEMO_CONTROLS=1
